  "id": "COMPOUND:23649 - PROTEIN:5942",
  "verbalization": "Caffeic Acid 3,4-Dihydroxyphenethyl Ester is implicated in the targeting of SNU-387, a cell line that is also a target of multiple compounds, including (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol and Eryngiolide A. All these compounds ultimately target Tankyrase-2, suggesting a shared mechanism of action involving Tankyrase-2 as a downstream effector. The evidence indicates that Caffeic Acid 3,4-Dihydroxyphenethyl Ester may act through a common pathway that leads to the activation or regulation of Tankyrase-2, possibly by modulating its activity in the cellular context. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of Tankyrase-2 in the biological response to this compound, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
